[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/less/less.js/issues/comments/75042971","html_url":"https://github.com/less/less.js/issues/2461#issuecomment-75042971","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/less/less.js/issues/2461","id":75042971,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc1MDQyOTcx","user":{"login":"tomek-he-him","id":4624660,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjQ2NjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4624660?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomek-he-him","html_url":"https://github.com/tomek-he-him","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomek-he-him/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomek-he-him/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomek-he-him/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomek-he-him/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomek-he-him/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomek-he-him/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomek-he-him/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomek-he-him/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomek-he-him/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-02-19T12:19:08Z","updated_at":"2015-02-23T08:07:29Z","body":"AD 1. From what I can see, upon running `$ lessc input.less` stderr is empty. How about using that for displaying CLI errors and warnings?\n\nAD 1. I use gulp-less for building my project. It'd be great if that logged something when it sees a warning. Perhaps `less.render(input, callback)` could pass some special kind of error to the `callback` when it wants to communicate a warning? So that tools like gulp-less can pick it up.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/less/less.js/issues/comments/75042971/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eye