,"organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-02-19T13:06:38Z","updated_at":"2015-02-19T13:07:09Z","body":"At first glance I'd rather suggest to put warnings as comments into the generated CSS itself (i.e. `stdout` instead of `stderr`... Otherwise (if I'm not mistaken) it will broke stuff using `lessc input.less > output.css`).\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/less/less.js/issues/comments/75048663/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"seven-phases-max","id":5304376,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMDQzNzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5304376?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max","html_url":"https://github.com/seven-phases-max","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/less/less.js/issues/comments/75370004","html_url":"https://github.com/less/less.js/issues/2461#issuecomment-75370004","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/less/less.js/issues/2461","id":75370004,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc1MzcwMDA0","user":{"login":"SomMeri","id":618879,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxODg3OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/618879?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri","html_url":"https://github.com/SomMeri","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-02-21T12:41:16Z","updated_at":"2015-02-21T12:41:16Z","body":"`lessc input.less > output.css` redirects only stdout. If you want to redirect both stderr and stdout you have to do `lessc input.less &> output.css`.\n\nI think it is more correct to put errors and warnings into stderr, it would allow scripts to check for warnings and errors easily. lessc will be often run by tools instead of manually and having to parse output.css for warnings and errors is ugly.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/less/less.js/issues/comments/75370004/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"SomMeri","id":618879,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxODg3OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/618879?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri","html_url":"https://github.com/SomMeri","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/less/less.js/issues/comments/75378546","html_url":"https://github.com/less/less.js/issues/2461#issuecomment-75378546","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/less/less.js/issues/2461","id":75378546,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc1Mzc4NTQ2","user":{"login":"seven-phases-max","id":5304376,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMDQzNzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5304376?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max","html_url":"https://github.com/seven-phases-max","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-02-21T16:15:55Z","updated_at":"2015-02-21T16:52:25Z","body":"Well, that's not just  `input.less > output.css`. There're many editors/IDEs that capture output of external tools and in most it's just imposible to get both `stderr` and `stdout` (for instance the one I use won't log `stderr` if `errcode = 0`), i.e. since warnings are not errors, spamming `stderr` w/o an actual error may break common \"piping stuff\" conventions in many ways.\n\n> having to parse output.css for warnings and errors is ugly.\n\nMany tools interpret any output in `stderr` as a error and stop.\n\n---\n\nTo be more specific my idea is not to replace `stderr` with comments in CSS everywhere but only use it if no output file specified. In other words, we should have a way to see warnings somehow with just `lessc input.less` (maybe not by default but with certain cli-option) but can't use `stderr` for that since this will break tools that assume `lessc input.less` outputs either a error or valid CSS.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/less/less.js/issues/comments/75378546/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"seven-phases-max","id":5304376,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMDQzNzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5304376?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max","html_url":"https://github.com/seven-phases-max","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/less/less.js/issues/comments/75437271","html_url":"https://github.com/less/less.js/issues/2461#issuecomment-75437271","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/less/less.js/issues/2461","id":75437271,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc1NDM3Mjcx","user":{"login":"SomMeri","id":618879,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxODg3OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/618879?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri","html_url":"https://github.com/SomMeri","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-02-22T14:15:13Z","updated_at":"2015-02-22T14:15:13Z","body":"@seven-phases-max That is a good point. Out of curiosity, which tools do that? \n\nI got curious and tested gcc, python and javac compilers on windows. All three print both errors and warnings into stderr. They use exit code 1 when they encounter error and exit code 0 when they encounter warnings only. \n\nThat does not mean we have to do it the same way, just that it is the standard way. If too many tools in js/css word tend to misinterpret streams, it might make sense to go with them. But, I still think it is their bug and they should fix it :).\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/less/less.js/issues/comments/75437271/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"SomMeri","id":618879,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxODg3OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/618879?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri","html_url":"https://github.com/SomMeri","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomMeri/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":239757688,"node_id":"MDE0Ok1lbnRpb25lZEV2ZW50MjM5NzU3Njg4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/less/less.js/issues/events/239757688","actor":{"login":"seven-phases-max","id":5304376,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMDQzNzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5304376?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seven-phases-max","html_url":"https://github.com/seven-phases-max","followers_url":"https://api.gith